  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "14466302",
      "title": "Understanding Operators",
      "lectureOrder": 501,
      "videoOrder": 460,
      "sourceHash": "5303e9b46e6dde51ac0ea334386508fb536aaf700be91be61f30f63afeddeaa3",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 2.22,
          "end": 5.22,
          "en": "Instructor: Now it's all nice what we learned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 5.22,
          "end": 8.64,
          "en": "But there is one super important thing about observables",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 8.64,
          "end": 12.93,
          "en": "and the RxJS library that you absolutely have to know",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 12.93,
          "end": 15.72,
          "en": "and that would be Operators.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 15.72,
          "end": 19.92,
          "en": "Operators are the magic feature of the RxJS library",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 19.92,
          "end": 22.86,
          "en": "and they are the thing that really turn observables",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 22.86,
          "end": 25.56,
          "en": "into awesome constructs.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 25.56,
          "end": 27.93,
          "en": "If we have an observable and an observer",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 27.93,
          "end": 30,
          "en": "we of course get data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 30,
          "end": 32.4,
          "en": "and we listen to that with a subscription.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 32.4,
          "end": 34.11,
          "en": "That is what you learn.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 34.11,
          "end": 37.29,
          "en": "Now, however, sometimes you don't need the raw data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 37.29,
          "end": 40.05,
          "en": "You might want to transform it or filter",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 40.05,
          "end": 43.17,
          "en": "out certain data points and of course you could do all",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 43.17,
          "end": 45.33,
          "en": "of that inside of your subscription",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 45.33,
          "end": 48.21,
          "en": "or in the function you pass to your subscription.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 48.21,
          "end": 50.13,
          "en": "But there is a more elegant way.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 50.13,
          "end": 52.98,
          "en": "Instead of setting up that subscription like this",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 52.98,
          "end": 56.85,
          "en": "you can use builtin operators in between.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 56.85,
          "end": 59.31,
          "en": "That means that the data points, first of all",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 59.31,
          "end": 61.59,
          "en": "reach these operators that do something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 61.59,
          "end": 64.32,
          "en": "to the data and that something can be anything.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 64.32,
          "end": 67.35,
          "en": "There are tons of builtin operators",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 67.35,
          "end": 70.83,
          "en": "and then you subscribe to the result of these operators.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 70.83,
          "end": 72.78,
          "en": "Now let me show you a concrete example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 72.78,
          "end": 73.98,
          "en": "that makes that clearer.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 75.87,
          "end": 78.87,
          "en": "Let's say here, in our application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 78.87,
          "end": 83.87,
          "en": "we of course get our values 0,1,2,3 before we get an error.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 84.63,
          "end": 87.15,
          "en": "And let's say I'm not interested in these values",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 87.15,
          "end": 90.12,
          "en": "but I want to have some text that says something",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 90.12,
          "end": 94.11,
          "en": "like round one, round two, round three, and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 94.11,
          "end": 95.88,
          "en": "So in the end I want to use that count",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 95.88,
          "end": 99.78,
          "en": "add one and add the word round in front of it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 99.78,
          "end": 103.53999999999999,
          "en": "Now obviously what we can do is we can simply log, round",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 104.899,
          "end": 109.899,
          "en": "plus data plus one here, add extra parenthesis",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 110.19,
          "end": 114.18,
          "en": "around that so that it is really used as a calculation.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 114.18,
          "end": 116.75999999999999,
          "en": "And if we do that well we see round one, two, three",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 116.75999999999999,
          "end": 118.5,
          "en": "and so on being locked here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 118.5,
          "end": 122.16,
          "en": "Now nothing wrong with that and for simple transformations",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 122.16,
          "end": 124.29,
          "en": "like this one, of course that makes sense",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 124.29,
          "end": 127.92,
          "en": "but the more complex your logic gets",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 127.92,
          "end": 130.2,
          "en": "the nicer it might be to not care",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 130.2,
          "end": 133.47,
          "en": "about that here in the place where you subscribe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 133.47,
          "end": 136.07999999999998,
          "en": "But in an earlier place.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 136.07999999999998,
          "end": 138.9,
          "en": "So here I'll revert this to just logging the data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 138.9,
          "end": 142.65,
          "en": "and I wanna change the format in which that data arrives.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 142.65,
          "end": 144.51,
          "en": "And obviously we could do that directly here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 144.51,
          "end": 146.73,
          "en": "where we create our observable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 146.73,
          "end": 149.37,
          "en": "But what if you don't own the observable?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 149.37,
          "end": 152.67000000000002,
          "en": "What if you wanted to change the route prints, for example?",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 152.67000000000002,
          "end": 154.45,
          "en": "You can't change the original code",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 155.57999999999998,
          "end": 159.483,
          "en": "and that is where operators are important.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 160.32,
          "end": 162.51,
          "en": "You can use them on any observable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 162.51,
          "end": 165.493,
          "en": "like our custom interval observable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 165.493,
          "end": 168.36,
          "en": "by calling a method called pipe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 168.36,
          "end": 171.69,
          "en": "Now every observable has a pipe method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 171.69,
          "end": 174.9,
          "en": "The pipe method is built into RxJS.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 174.9,
          "end": 179.34,
          "en": "Now you can import observables not from the RxJS package",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 179.34,
          "end": 183.72,
          "en": "but from RxJS slash operators and there are tons",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 183.72,
          "end": 187.35,
          "en": "of builtin operators like the map operator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 187.35,
          "end": 190.47,
          "en": "which is one of the operators you'll use more often.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 190.47,
          "end": 194.49,
          "en": "As a side note, if you want to learn more",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 194.49,
          "end": 198.36,
          "en": "about RxJS and operators hands on",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 198.36,
          "end": 200.34,
          "en": "you can visit my homepage academind.com",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 200.34,
          "end": 202.77,
          "en": "and there on the learn JavaScript",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 202.77,
          "end": 206.07,
          "en": "you'll find a complete series on RxJS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 206.07,
          "end": 210.36,
          "en": "which introduces you to RxJS and to operators as well.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 210.36,
          "end": 213.03,
          "en": "It uses slightly older syntax.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 213.03,
          "end": 216.18,
          "en": "RxJS was changed in the meantime, which by the way",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 216.18,
          "end": 218.57999999999998,
          "en": "all the cover on my page,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 218.57999999999998,
          "end": 221.76,
          "en": "here in RxJS six what changed, but the core idea",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 221.76,
          "end": 225,
          "en": "and the explanation about these operators still applies.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 225,
          "end": 229.02,
          "en": "That can be very useful for learning more about RxJS",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 229.02,
          "end": 231.99,
          "en": "but that's just a side note back to our code here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 231.99,
          "end": 233.49,
          "en": "So we have that pipe method",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 233.49,
          "end": 236.28,
          "en": "and we're importing map here and map, as I mentioned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 236.28,
          "end": 239.16,
          "en": "is one of the more important operators.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 239.16,
          "end": 243.33,
          "en": "Now we simply call map as a function inside of pipe here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 243.33,
          "end": 246.84,
          "en": "And map in turn takes a function as an argument.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 246.84,
          "end": 248.94,
          "en": "So an anonymous function here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 248.94,
          "end": 253.14,
          "en": "if you want that however gets an argument",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 253.14,
          "end": 255.24,
          "en": "that anonymous function gets an argument",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 255.24,
          "end": 258.45,
          "en": "and that is the data you would otherwise get here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 258.45,
          "end": 260.55,
          "en": "in your first subscribe callback.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 260.55,
          "end": 262.98,
          "en": "So in that first function you pass to subscribe",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 262.98,
          "end": 264.36,
          "en": "it's the current data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 264.36,
          "end": 267.81,
          "en": "of your observable that's being emitted by that observable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 267.81,
          "end": 270.72,
          "en": "So we get that data here and in map we now have to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 270.72,
          "end": 274.59000000000003,
          "en": "return new data that can of course be the unchanged",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 274.59000000000003,
          "end": 277.2,
          "en": "old data, in which case that map operator",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 277.2,
          "end": 278.73,
          "en": "is totally useless.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 278.73,
          "end": 280.86,
          "en": "But it can also be transformed data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 280.86,
          "end": 285.86,
          "en": "like for example, round plus data plus one.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 287.1,
          "end": 289.8,
          "en": "So what we previously did right in console lock",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 289.8,
          "end": 291.36,
          "en": "now we're doing it here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 291.36,
          "end": 294.45,
          "en": "We just have to be clear about the format of data here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 294.45,
          "end": 295.8,
          "en": "as it seems.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 295.8,
          "end": 298.68,
          "en": "You can of course do that by wrapping data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 298.68,
          "end": 301.68,
          "en": "and parenthesis here in the argument list, adding a colon",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 301.68,
          "end": 304.47,
          "en": "after it and making it clear that this will be a number",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 304.47,
          "end": 306.75,
          "en": "and now if you're safe that it will compile.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 306.75,
          "end": 308.88,
          "en": "But what you'll see in your project now is still",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 308.88,
          "end": 310.41,
          "en": "the old output.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 310.41,
          "end": 313.32,
          "en": "The reason for data is let's wait for this to complete.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 313.32,
          "end": 318,
          "en": "The reason for data is that this is applied, but we still",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 318,
          "end": 320.88,
          "en": "subscribe to this observable and this does not",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 320.88,
          "end": 323.43,
          "en": "change data inside of the observable.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 323.43,
          "end": 327.93,
          "en": "Instead, it only changes the data we get after pipe.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 327.93,
          "end": 331.11,
          "en": "So what we would have to do here is simply we have to",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 331.11,
          "end": 336.11,
          "en": "take that and replace our observable here with it.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 336.65999999999997,
          "end": 340.32,
          "en": "So the concrete observable, we're subscribing to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 340.32,
          "end": 342.96,
          "en": "Now if we do that, so if we have our observable",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 342.96,
          "end": 345.18,
          "en": "then we pipe the data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 345.18,
          "end": 348.09000000000003,
          "en": "So we add a couple of operators in this case",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 348.09000000000003,
          "end": 349.53,
          "en": "the map operator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 349.53,
          "end": 352.53,
          "en": "Then when we subscribe thereafter we'll get that mapped.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 352.53,
          "end": 356.4,
          "en": "So that changed data and now when we save this,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 356.4,
          "end": 360.63,
          "en": "we'll see that that we get round 1, 2, 3 and so on.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 360.63,
          "end": 362.37,
          "en": "So this is the map operator.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 362.37,
          "end": 366.09,
          "en": "And again, just before this is kind of a constructed example",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 366.09,
          "end": 368.58,
          "en": "here it is of course more useful.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 368.58,
          "end": 371.37,
          "en": "For example, if you're fetching complex data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 371.37,
          "end": 374.04,
          "en": "from a web server and you want to transform that data",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 374.04,
          "end": 375.78,
          "en": "before you use it in a component",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 375.78,
          "end": 378.09,
          "en": "and that is something we'll do later too",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 378.09,
          "end": 380.91,
          "en": "but the core idea is the same with pipe,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 380.91,
          "end": 383.16,
          "en": "we can add one or more operators.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 383.16,
          "end": 384.45,
          "en": "If you have more than one",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 384.45,
          "end": 388.38,
          "en": "you'll simply add them as arguments here to the pipe method.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 388.38,
          "end": 390.72,
          "en": "So the pipe method takes an unlimited amount",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 390.72,
          "end": 394.5,
          "en": "of arguments and each argument would be an operator imported",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 394.5,
          "end": 397.89,
          "en": "from RxJS operators and you can add as many as you want",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 397.89,
          "end": 399.96,
          "en": "and they will execute after each other",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 399.96,
          "end": 402.51,
          "en": "and do different kinds of stuff on the data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 135,
          "start": 402.51,
          "end": 405.96,
          "en": "This is map of course, for example, you could also filter.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 136,
          "start": 405.96,
          "end": 407.25,
          "en": "That's our operator indeed.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 137,
          "start": 407.25,
          "end": 409.92,
          "en": "So let's use that just to demonstrate one more.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 138,
          "start": 409.92,
          "end": 414.92,
          "en": "Now there are dozens by the way, besides using my page here.",
